      "scientific_basis": [
        "The original owner was imported specifically as MediaDive362 Phytone. MediaDive125 names Phytone peptone; TOGO M2989 explicitly says phytone(BBL). These independently agree on the named Phytone preparation rather than arbitrary hydrolyzed vegetable protein.",
        "Current MicrO0001795 is nonobsolete, names Phytone peptone, explicitly identifies the BBL/Difco trademark, and cites the BD manual definition of papaic soybean meal digest. Its explicit definition-source resolves the intended concept more narrowly than generic soy peptone.",
        "The parent returned by current OLS is MICRO0000181 soy peptone, not a barley-specific parent. Both term texts contain the contradictory Hordeum vulgare parenthesis. That annotation error is retained as an evidence limitation; it is not adopted as barley identity. No assertion is made that the ontology has been repaired.",
        "The current manufacturer technical guide, p33 and product comparison, distinguishes Phytone, Phytone UF, Difco Soytone, Bacto Soytone and Soy Peptone100. A common soybean origin does not equate these product lines."
      ],
      "allowable_deltas": [
        {
          "field": "identifier",
          "from": "FOODON:03315720",
          "to": "MICRO:0001795",
          "condition": "After exact term/current-owner native validation; unchanged existing owner path."
        },
        {
          "field": "ontology_mapping",
          "to": {
            "ontology_id": "MICRO:0001795",
            "ontology_label": "Phytone peptone",
            "ontology_source": "MICRO",
            "mapping_quality": "EXACT_MATCH"
          },
          "evidence": "Claim-specific exact product/ontology evidence, retaining prior broad mapping as explicitly superseded history."
        },
        {
          "field": "supplied_form",
          "to": "Named Phytone peptone/BBL or BD-BBL product provenance; no invented modern SKU, UF status, batch formula or universal supplier equivalence."
        },
        {
          "field": "synonyms",
          "to": "Preserve Phytone, reviewed Phytone peptone and phytone(BBL) source forms with their original sources. They are identity-bearing at this product scope; do not call RAW_TEXT nonresolving."
        }
      ],
      "coupling": [
        "On both active Soy_Peptone alternatives, disposition the exact original tokens Phytone peptone; Phytone peptone(BD-BBL); Soytone(BD-Difco) or Phytone peptone(BD-BBL) so they no longer claim exact identity of the Soy owner. Preserve original spelling/source. The first two name a specific distinct product; the third is a choice between products, not one identity-bearing name.",
        "Use cited REJECTED_LABEL dispositions for these false broader/narrower or alternative-product identity claims, rather than hiding them with export-only SUPPRESS. Do not generalize this to every Soytone/Bacto or peptic-digest token without its own review.",
        "No baseline component references to FOODON03315720 were found by explicit enumeration of all2956 frozen records; that absence does not authorize mass migration of recipe-membership or historical SSSOM rows keyed to the shared ID. Keep Bacto_Soytone tombstone/representative history intact."
      ],
      "alternatives_rejected": {
        "local_Phytone": "An exact material-specific term exists and is supported; the local fallback is unnecessary under section3 step1.",
        "generic_FOODON_exact": "Hydrolyzed vegetable protein does not identify the named Phytone product.",
        "merge_Soy_family": "Shared broad identifier and historical benign-duplicate comment504 are not product identity evidence."
      },
      "remaining_questions": [
        "No human choice of Phytone namespace is needed on this evidence. Current Soy-family owner scope and aliases outside the three named tokens remain separate coupled decisions. Upstream botanical annotation correction is an ontology-maintenance issue, not a reason to copy barley biology."
      ],
      "rubric": {
        "chemistry": "Do not assign formula, molecular weight, CAS, structure or pure-compound chemistry to these complex biological/product mixtures. No new chemistry is supported here.",
        "roles": "No ingredient role, growth phenotype, supplier interchangeability, assay outcome or release approval is conferred.",
        "occurrences": "Preserve every origin case and occurrence ID. Historical counts and broad-ID memberships are provenance, not reviewed material identity or approval. Do not transfer memberships by old shared identifier.",
