      "scientific_basis": [
        "Authentic history created UNMAPPED0507 from MediaDive1769 before a later alias backfill added three supplier spellings. The exact MediaDive1769 page records BD-Difco3uses; fresh JCM481,482,612 each explicitly name BD-DifcoRCM38g. This is source continuity, not worker/hash precedence.",
        "The Difco/BBL manual2nd edition lists nine approximate formula constituents: peptone10,beefextract10,yeastextract3,dextrose5,sodiumchloride5,solublestarch1,cysteineHCl0.5,sodiumacetate3,agar0.5 grams per liter. It explicitly allows adjustment/supplementation for performance. The printed peptone is not a justified Tryptose subtype.",
        "NBRC902 explicitly requires OxoidCM0149 38g,water1L,optional additional agar15g. That source does not name BD-Difco. Current OxoidIFU0539 CM0149B/T has eight printed ingredients including yeast13g/L and no beefextract, with agar0.5g/L. CM0151 is a separate agar product/table.",
        "DSMZ634 allowsBD-BBL,Oxoid orMerck. Permitted functional alternatives do not establish identical product compositions. Current manufacturer formulas must not be retroactively attached to all historical revisions."
      ],
